{
  "source": "research/charset.md §5, §5.1, §5.3 — IBM 1410 Principles of Operation A22-0526-3 pp.6-7 (Figure 2 and its footnotes), p.67; IBM 1403 Component Description GA24-3073 pp.5-6, 25, 27",
  "note": "The 1403 CHAIN's 48 graphics for all 64 BCD codes, on both published arrangements. This is NOT bcd.ts's glyph column: that is the 1415 TYPEBALL's 64 characters, one per code. Twelve codes have no slug on either arrangement and print BLANK; three codes print a slug that belongs to a different code. `a` and `h` are the printed character, or \"\" where the code has no slug (prints blank). `octal` is the manual's own two-digit BA8421 octal and is the key the test asserts on; `hollerith` is charset.md §2's card code, carried so a reviewer can cross-check the row against Figure 2 without a second lookup. Rows are in collating order (charset.md §4), the same order bcd.ts prints, so the two tables can be read side by side.",
  "caution": "charset.md §5.3, verbatim: SimH's `mem_to_ascii[64]` in `i7010_sys.c` renders 12 (`BA`) as `+`, 12-4-8 as `)`, 0-4-8 as `(`, 4-8 as `'` and 3-8 as `=` — i.e. the H-chain glyphs. An emulator that copies SimH's table inherits the H arrangement, not the A2 arrangement the 1410 PoO assumes.",
  "sets": {
    "A": "A-Z, 0-9, & . ⌑ - $ * / , % # @ ‡  (26 + 10 + 12 = 48 graphics; the commercial A2 / AN arrangement)",
    "H": "A-Z, 0-9, + . ) - $ * / , ( = ' ‡  (the COBOL/FORTRAN H2 / HN arrangement)"
  },
  "dualed": [
    { "octal": "60", "hollerith": "12", "a": "&", "h": "+" },
    { "octal": "74", "hollerith": "12-4-8", "a": "⌑", "h": ")" },
    { "octal": "34", "hollerith": "0-4-8", "a": "%", "h": "(" },
    { "octal": "13", "hollerith": "3-8", "a": "#", "h": "=" },
    { "octal": "14", "hollerith": "4-8", "a": "@", "h": "'" }
  ],
  "blankOnBothChains": {
    "note": "charset.md §5, verbatim: \"Codes on neither 48-character chain: [ < GM ] ; Δ WS \\ SM : > √ — these print blank.\" Twelve codes.",
    "octals": ["75", "76", "77", "55", "56", "57", "35", "36", "37", "15", "16", "17"],
    "names": ["left bracket", "less than", "group mark", "right bracket", "semicolon", "delta (mode change)", "word separator", "backslash", "segment mark", "colon", "greater than", "tape mark (radical)"]
